1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,780
Before you can fix something, you need to understand what's broken.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:09,360
In this case, what's broken is approximately everything. They say knowledge is power.

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:16,780
In this case, knowledge is mostly just depressing. But you need it, the way you need to know your house is on fire before

4
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:26,840
you can put it out. The Daily Body Count. Every day, 150,000 humans die from disease and aging.

5
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:32,860
That's fifty nine-elevens. Per day. Including weekends and holidays.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,200
When one thing kills 3,000 people, it's a tragedy and you start wars.

7
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:47,980
When diseases kill 50 times that every day, it's called "natural causes," which is Latin for "you couldn't be bothered.".

8
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:55,220
After the first nine-eleven, America invaded two countries and spent two trillion dollars.

9
00:00:55,940 --> 00:01:00,820
After the fifty daily nine-elevens, humanity shrugs and wonders what's for lunch.

10
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:08,720
Where the Money Goes. Killing each other: two point seven two trillion dollars per year.

11
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,320
Curing diseases: sixty-seven point five billion dollars per year.

12
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:20,260
The real bottleneck isn't research funding. It's testing which treatments actually work.

13
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:29,740
Governments worldwide spend four point five billion dollars annually on clinical trials versus two point seven two trillion

14
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:39,180
dollars on weapons. That's a six hundred and four ratio, which in technical terms is called "having your priorities backwards.".

15
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:47,780
On Medical Research. Since 1970, the N.I.H. has spent over one trillion dollars studying diseases.

16
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:58,900
Diseases cured: Zero. Of its forty-seven billion dollar annual budget, only 3.3 percent goes to actual drug trials in humans.

17
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:06,140
The other 97 percent goes to studying mice, building buildings, and publishing papers nobody reads.

18
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:11,100
The system operates at 2 percent of its potential capacity to save lives.

19
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:18,560
On the F.D.A. The F.D.A. makes drugs eighty-two times more expensive than necessary.

20
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:25,820
It takes 14 years and two point six billion dollars to get a drug from discovery to patient.

21
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:32,520
That's longer than it took to build the pyramids. The pharaohs didn't have to file quarterly progress reports in triplicate.

22
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:38,880
Ninety-five percent of diseases have zero approved treatments because the F.D.A.

23
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:44,220
is excellent at preventing any drugs from reaching people. On What War Costs.

24
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:50,880
Humanity spends two point seven two trillion dollars every year on war.

25
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:58,020
That works out to three hundred forty dollars per human on Earth for death tools.

26
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:08,320
This budget includes: Nuclear bombs (13,000 of them, because 12,999 wouldn't destroy Earth thoroughly enough).

27
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:15,480
Bullets (many). A.I. murder robots (the future is here and it's disappointing).

28
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:24,920
Fighter jets that cost more than hospitals. Submarines (one submarine equals one thousand cancer research labs).

29
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:34,260
Probably some kind of earthquake machine. Your personal lifetime contribution to the murder budget is seventy-four thousand,

30
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:39,600
two hundred fifty-nine dollars. You could have bought a really nice casket instead.

31
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:44,060
Or, and this is just a thought, not needed a casket quite so soon.

32
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:51,000
The interesting thing about having 13,000 nuclear warheads is that after the first few hundred, you're just showing off.

33
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:57,840
You can only destroy Earth once. The remaining 12,700 are for what, exactly?

34
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:04,840
Destroying Earth's ghost? It's like buying 13,000 fire extinguishers for a one-room flat.

35
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:11,220
At some point, the fire extinguishers are the fire hazard. On What Disease Costs.

36
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:17,600
Disease extracts one hundred and nine trillion dollars from humanity annually.

37
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:24,230
That includes 10 million cancer deaths per year and 2 billion people living with chronic diseases.

38
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:32,280
Depression alone affects a billion people, costing five trillion dollars in lost "wanting to exist.".

39
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:37,720
If disease were a country, it would be the richest country on Earth by a factor of ten.

40
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:43,120
Unfortunately, disease doesn't have a flag or an army, so nobody invades it.

41
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:50,860
Out of two point four billion people suffering from chronic disease, only one point nine million patients per year get to

42
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:56,220
participate in clinical trials. That's zero point zero seven nine two percent.

43
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:03,360
Half would volunteer if asked. You're turning away ninety-nine point six percent of willing participants.

44
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:12,720
On Democracy. A Princeton study found zero percent correlation between what the public wants and what policies get enacted.

45
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:22,540
Zero. Not "low." Not "disappointing." Zero. Your democracy has the same correlation with your preferences as a coin flip

46
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:30,660
has with your breakfast order. When military contractors want one hundred billion dollars, they spend fifty-five million

47
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:36,180
dollars lobbying for it. That's a one thousand eight hundred thirteen percent return on investment.

48
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:42,000
When you want healthcare, you have approximately zero dollars to lobby with.

49
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:48,280
You spent it all on healthcare. Or you're dead, which significantly reduces your lobbying capacity.

50
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:53,540
Meanwhile, the people who regulate industries used to work for those industries.

51
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,720
They'll work for them again after they're done "regulating."

52
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:02,340
It's called the revolving door, and it spins in one direction: toward money.

53
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:10,900
On the Fixed Pie. Money isn't real, but resources are. Earth has 8 billion human brains.

54
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:15,800
Every M.I.T. graduate building missiles is not curing cancer.

55
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:21,420
Every brilliant physicist designing warheads is not designing M.R.I.

56
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:28,640
machines. You have a fixed number of geniuses. You are using them to build things that kill other geniuses.

57
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:37,040
Switzerland spends zero point seven percent of G.D.P. on military and has ninety-three thousand dollars G.D.P.

58
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:43,820
per capita. America spends three point five percent and has seventy-six thousand dollars.

59
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:47,080
The solution isn't to print more money for medical research.

60
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:54,160
The solution is to change the ratio. Take money from the killing budget, give it to the not-dying budget.

61
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:59,220
This is called "arithmetic," which is apparently a controversial field of mathematics.

62
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:08,480
What This Means. 150,000 humans die daily from disease and aging, many eventually avoidable.

63
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:13,540
Two point seven two trillion dollars spent annually on weapons.

64
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:20,880
Sixty-seven point five billion dollars spent annually on curing all diseases combined.

65
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:25,620
Six hundred and four weapons-to-clinical-trials spending ratio.

66
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:34,120
Zero diseases cured in fifty years. Zero percent correlation between public preferences and policy.

67
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:40,840
You are dying while reading this. If this seems bad, that's because you're paying attention.

68
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:46,640
The good news is you're going to fix it. The bad news is it requires doing things.

69
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:56,940
The weird news is you'll get rich doing it. What's Next. The following chapters explain each problem in detail: The Daily

70
